{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And the hands of Moshe grew heavy.</b> Because he was remiss in the commandment and appointed another in his stead — his hands grew heavy." "<b>And they took.</b> Aharon and Hur." "<b>A stone, and they placed it under him.</b> And he did not sit for himself on a cushion and pillow. He said: Israel is immersed in suffering — I too will be with them in suffering (Ta'anit 11)." "<b>And his hands were faith.</b> And the hands of Moshe were in faith — spread out to heaven in faithful and established prayer." "<b>Until the sun came.</b> For the Amalekites would calculate the hours by astrology — at which hour they are victorious — and Moshe set the sun awry and mixed up the hours for them (Tanchuma)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:52.858680907Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}